@startbpmn BP20_CloseBearing
lang en             ' the only stakeholder is the Software Architect, who authored the sources in English

output L1 "01_detailed/BP20_CloseBearing.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP20_CloseBearing.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - LEAVING THE PRODUCT was drawn by no process. BP01.09 closes it, but it is reached only from
'     the refusal path of a launch that cannot continue, so an ordinary quit had no drawn path:
'     SA 2026-10-17 ("add BP to close bearing")
'   - nothing of the user's is pending at the close: every gesture has been committed or left as a
'     draft, and a draft survives the close and is there on the next launch: BR-121, BR-32, BP19
'   - the remembered interface state is restored on a launch onto usable data, so the close leaves
'     it standing rather than writing it away: BR-92, BP01
'   - the close SETTLES NOTHING: no check-out is made, nothing is archived, no task is touched and
'     the date in play is not advanced. The span since the last check-out stays open and the next
'     check-out takes it, exactly as it does across a rollover: BR-33, BR-44, BP13, BP14
'   - nothing is asked before it closes: a confirmation guards against losing work, and there is no
'     work to lose - what is half-written is a draft by then: BR-121, DRW-02, SA 2026-10-17
'   - this is not the start-up refusal, which closes the product as the ONLY way on from a launch
'     that cannot continue; that path is BP01's and keeps its own call site: BP01, BR-80, BR-122
'
' Scope: this process ends a session. Starting one is BP01; what the user did in between is the
' other eighteen.
'
' Call-site collapsing: closing is ONE operation, drawn by two processes - BP01.09 on the refusal
' path and BP20.01 here. Which System Interaction both resolve to is a Design decision recorded in
' si-binding.yaml, never a rename (ADR-069).

pool "User" {
  start "Nothing more to do in Bearing"
  :Leave Bearing;
  note "Nothing is pending: every gesture has been committed or left as a draft, and a draft is there again on the next launch. Nothing is settled either - the span since the last check-out stays open."
  send "Close Bearing" to closeIn
  end "Bearing closed"
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Close requested" as closeIn
  call "BP20.01_CloseBearing" "Close Bearing" {
    :Shut the product down;
    rule BR-121
    rule BR-92
  }
  note "One-way: nothing waits for the shutdown to be reported. The drafts and the remembered interface state stay where they are, and the next launch restores them."
  end "Product shut down"
}

@endbpmn
